  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 207 PM EDT Thu Aug 13 2026\n\nUpper ridge currently extending through the Plains with downstream \nwest/northwest flow aloft across the Great Lakes. Convective\ncomplexes continue to ride along the primary instability axis \nto our south and west. The upper ridge will gradually shift east\ninto this weekend, deamplifying a bit as a shortwave trough \nmoves through. Upper ridge will flex again to our west early \nnext week, with northwest flow resuming over the Great Lakes. \n\nFairly benign weather through Friday with increasing influence of \ndrier and more stable air, as high pressure builds in from the \nnorthwest.  A small chance of an early evening shower over northeast \nlower along a lake breeze boundary, but any activity would be \nisolated and dissipate quickly.  Some patchy fog again tonight, \nalthough decreasing soil moisture and an overall drier atmosphere \nshould limit the extent.  Quiet weather continues on Friday, despite \nanother shortwave passing to our east, with limited moisture making \nany shower development difficult.  \n\nUnsettled weather still in store for the weekend, although more \nrecent model runs are further south with the shortwave energy \nand surface reflection. Although deeper moisture on the backside\nof departing high pressure will push toward the area on \nSaturday, it will initially have to fight a relatively dry \nairmass. Eventually, the deeper moisture (PWATs 200% of normal) \nwill win out and surge northward into our area Saturday night \ninto early Sunday, which is when we will see the best chance of \nprecipitation. The trends have been drier overall in recent \nmodel runs and the heavy rain threat looks to be focusing more \nover central/southern Michigan. Unfortunately, this could keep \nmuch needed steadier rains out of northern Michigan. Cold front \nsweeps across the area by later Sunday with deep layer drying. \n\nAdditional shortwave energy in fast moving northwest upper flow will \nbring unsettled weather and shower chances back to the area for \nTuesday and Wednesday. Temperatures a little cooler from Sunday into \nearly next week, although still comfortable 70s for most areas.",
